A||||19||jch82||Wind Deflector For Sunroof||||5||
Z||000000||jch82||05-04-2001||12:11 AM||||Does anyone have one? If so, what kind and where did you get it? Pics?<P>I installed a roof with a sunroof because my previous roof didnt have one. I put my friend's glass in and there is definitely wind coming in from the front of the sunroof glass. I figure a deflector would be the best bet....Any info would be great!<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierofreek2001||05-04-2001||12:42 AM||||the wind deflector only goes on when the sunroof is off... what will work sometimes to stop some wind noise is to open the sun roof . that way the wind doesnt go underneath the glass and into the interior, it rises over and above....    if this doesnt make sense, its because its 1 in the morning...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>steve||||reg||1
Z||000002||sully5||05-04-2001||12:55 AM||||Josh, you should also check the hardware on the glass if you have not already. The front tabs should have a plastic like coating on them, and the 4 mounting points have rubber bushings that like to rot out. These pieces are still available from the dealer. Redid mine last spring. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||WampusCat||05-04-2001||07:55 AM||||I've got a different problem.  The sunroof wont stay open when I go over a bump in the road, which is every few seconds in the city.  Is there a way to adjust the latch mech. or does it have to be replaced?||||reg||1
Z||000004||sully5||05-04-2001||08:51 AM||||Wampus, I cannot remember if there is any adjsutment to that latch or not. I cannot remember there being any. Sorry I can't be any help. Sully||||reg||1
Z||000005||Max The Chainsaw||05-04-2001||09:04 AM||||Wampus, I had a similar problem with my 86 Coupe. I found out the latch wasn't opening fully. If I juggle it side to side when opening it, it would open another 1/2 inch. Wouldn't fall down then. Might give it a try.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||thomas_l||05-04-2001||10:31 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jch82:<BR><B>Does anyone have one? If so, what kind and where did you get it? Pics?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>After driving mine around with the roof out noticing how windy it was, I read the answer right on this forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">. Under the hood of the factory sunroof car is a mysterious piece of plastic that looks like some trim snapped into holders on the cowl. On another thread it was pointed out to me that this is the wind deflector and the clips fit into the roof slots where the tabs on the glass top go. They also pointed out the handy foam pads that are there to support and store the glass (over the spare) when it is not in the roof. Boy did I feel stupid  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I had stored my top in the top section of the trunk and was griping about it getting stuck under the weatherstrip. I drove my Fiero to work today so I can try out my wind deflector this afternoon. If your car doesn't have the item try looking in the junkyard. The one I have been going to has 4-5 Fieros and I know I have seen one or two of the deflectors.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fearlessdata.com/fiero/87GT_small.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Ken Wittlief||05-04-2001||10:39 AM||||I almost did something really stupid yesterday. I had the sunroof in the front trunk, and the wind deflector on the roof, and I was looking to see where my coolant leak was coming from, so I set the sunroof back on top of the car, just for a minute. Not hooked in, just sitting on top of the wind deflector.<P>Then I got distracted and forgot. An hour later I started driving down the street, and wondered why the sunroof was making so much wind noise!<P>  Good thing I didnt take off down my street like a batouttahell!<P>  I wonder if anyone has ever lost their sunroof from doing this.||||reg||1
Z||000008||JSocha||05-04-2001||10:42 AM||||It sounded to me like JCH82 just installed a sunroof into his vehicle (which originally and apparently had none) and is using his friends sunroof glass.  I've read it several time now just to make sure.<P>Or maybe...just maybe I'm English illiterate!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>If this is the case, he won't have the wind deflector as I do not recall GM (or for that matter other car manufacturers) making this a "standard" issue part for non sunroof vehicles.  And if this is the case, let me know as I may know where to find one.<P>Otherwise, you may have to find out who the manufacturer of your particular sunroof is and contact them for the deflector.  <P>If it was a "Fiero" sunroof off of another donor Fiero refitted to your Fiero then try Ebay or somebody on this post should have and/or know where to find one.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jnjsochasig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Ken Wittlief||05-04-2001||10:45 AM||||In that case the tabs to store the sunroof on in the front trunk may not be there either?||||reg||1
Z||000010||JSocha||05-04-2001||11:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>In that case the tabs to store the sunroof on in the front trunk may not be there either?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Huh?  Good point!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||sqoach||05-04-2001||11:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>In that case the tabs to store the sunroof on in the front trunk may not be there either?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>True.<BR>I'm pretty sure my car didn't come with a sunroof because those tabs are gone and so are the two pad thingies on the underside of the hood. So you'll probably have to get those too.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000012||MooCow||05-04-2001||11:42 AM||||I think that he is talking about something different.  I think he is looking for something you can use with the sun glass in.  This way it would deflect the air over and then no noise.  Anyone know what I am talking about now??  Anyone have one??<P>                                Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000013||sqoach||05-04-2001||11:48 AM||||I guess I didn't read this very closely the first time. You don't need a wind deflector with the sunroof in. If you have wind coming in with the glass on, then it must not be sealing very good.||||reg||1
Z||000014||mblackwell||05-04-2001||02:51 PM||||Does anyone have a pic of the factory wind deflector?  My car deosn't have one. I didn't know they existed until now. ||||reg||11
Z||000015||Ken Wittlief||05-04-2001||02:57 PM||||Its about an 1 1/4" high inthe middle, has a bit of a curve onthe front surface, spans the sunroof opening, and curves off round a few inches from each end<P>and it has a little bit of a bow to it, and two clips that snap in where the front tabs on the sunroof locks into the front of the roof.<P>   It looks like a little upsidedown front airdam when installed. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||JSocha||05-04-2001||03:00 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mblackwell:<BR><B>Does anyone have a pic of the factory wind deflector?  My car deosn't have one. I didn't know they existed until now. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Check the following thread by TheFiero64 <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007175.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/007175.html</A>  .<P>He has several pictures of the deflector in place when his sunroof was removed.  Its just a strip of modeled plastic with a couple of tabs on it.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jnjsochasig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 05-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||jch82||05-05-2001||10:02 PM||||WOW, look at all the responses! Haven't been on in a few days but thanks for all the replies....<P>What I was really thinking about is something like the wind deflectors they have for the driver/passenger windows but only for a sunroof. I have seen these on other cars and was wondering if anyone had used one for their fiero. They are plastic and usually attached with double-sided tape.<P>Thanks again for all the responses! BTW, I love this forum!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Josh   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I><p>[This message has been edited by jch82 (edited 05-05-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000018||Tryxalon||05-05-2001||11:28 PM||||The deflectors on the forward edge of the sunroof wouldn't work on a factory Fiero Sunroof since it opens in the back  &lt; or is completely out of the car. <P> Those are good for the Slide back Sunroofs on some cars. Ask the place where you got the sunroof?? <P>||||reg||5
Z||000019||Haze_Performance||05-06-2001||01:19 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>I almost did something really stupid yesterday. I had the sunroof in the front trunk, and the wind deflector on the roof, and I was looking to see where my coolant leak was coming from, so I set the sunroof back on top of the car, just for a minute. Not hooked in, just sitting on top of the wind deflector.<P>Then I got distracted and forgot. An hour later I started driving down the street, and wondered why the sunroof was making so much wind noise!<P>  Good thing I didnt take off down my street like a batouttahell!<P>  I wonder if anyone has ever lost their sunroof from doing this.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OK. I have a non Fiero story. My first car was a 1979 Fiat X19. (Targa) Well I was working on the car all day to get it running. It finally started...I was so happy I drove around the block. (Top Off) I stopped at a buddys house to show off the car and BAM!!! out of no where a rain storm hit. (HARD) I ran to the car & jumped in. Well in a hurry I kicked the fuse box... Most of the fuses poped out. (DAMN!!!) No lights or wipers!! I speed back to my house & flew in the driveway... I couldnt see that the wind blew the top into the driveway. (It was on the side of house when I left) Well SMASH!!!! I ran right over it!!,    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">        </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><I>If you want to add your Fiero to the collection, post or send me a photo. (Sent photos ONLY to: purplehazeracing@yahoo.com )</I><P><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A><BR><p>[This message has been 